================================================================================
assertion/fe-framework-test/ -- framework production builds
================================================================================

Each directory is a production build of a small sample app (the React
tic-tac-toe tutorial from react.dev, the Vue TodoMVC example, an Angular
tutorial app) and therefore bundles these libraries:

    React, ReactDOM, scheduler (react-19-1-releasebuild, via esm.sh in
      react-19-1-w-babel)          MIT, Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates.
    web-vitals (react-19-1-releasebuild/static/js/453.*.chunk.js)
                                   Apache-2.0, Copyright Google LLC
    Vue (vue-3-2-todo-dist)        MIT, Copyright (c) 2018-present, Yuxi (Evan) You
    Angular, zone.js (angular-v19-app-dist)
                                   MIT, Copyright (c) 2010-2025 Google LLC.
    @babel/standalone (react-19-1-w-babel/babel.min.js)
                                   MIT, Copyright (c) 2014-present Sebastian McKenzie and other contributors
    es-module-shims (react-19-1-w-babel/es-module-shims.js)
                                   MIT, Copyright (C) 2018-2021 Guy Bedford
    Create React App template and build output (react-19-1-releasebuild)
                                   MIT, Copyright (c) 2013-present, Facebook, Inc.
    Vue CLI template and build output (vue-3-2-todo-dist)
                                   MIT, Copyright (c) 2017-present, Yuxi (Evan) You
    webpack runtime (react-19-1-releasebuild, vue-3-2-todo-dist)
                                   MIT, Copyright JS Foundation and other contributors

The code of the React and Vue sample apps comes from documentation licensed
under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), compiled here into the builds:

    react-19-1-releasebuild, react-19-1-w-babel
        Tic-tac-toe tutorial, https://react.dev/learn/tutorial-tic-tac-toe
        Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates.
    vue-3-2-todo-dist
        TodoMVC example, https://github.com/vuejs/docs (src/examples/src/todomvc,
        removed from the documentation in 2025)
        Copyright (c) 2019-present, Yuxi (Evan) You and Vue documentation contributors

